>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TODA MICHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSURU EIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASAI, KIYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONEHARA, JUNICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMAI, TETSURO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TODA, MICHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSURU, EIJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Crystal polymorphism of 2-[4-[2-[[1s,2R]-2-hydroxy-2-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-1-methyl ethyl]amino]ethyl]phenoxy]acetic acid which has potent  beta 2 adrenergic receptor stimulating and  beta 3-adrenergic receptor stimulating effects, is useful in relieving a pain, promoting calculi removal, etc. in urinary lithiasis and shows intense diffraction peaks at 10.8, 19.1, 19.3, 19.8, 20.6 and 27.0 DEG  in the powder x-ray diffractometry pattern at a diffraction angle (2/ theta 0+/-0.1). It is produced by, for example, hydrolyzing ethyl 2-[4-[2-[[1S,2R]-2-hydroxy-2-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-1-methylethyl]amino]ethy]phenoxy]acetate phosphate by using sodium hydroxide, adding an aqueous solution of phosphoric acid at 40 DEG C or above to give the above compound, adding a solvent mixture comprising methanol with water or methanol and then stirring in a suspended state at from 40 DEG C to the reflux point for 30 minutes to several hours.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un polymorphisme cristallin d'acide 2-[4-[2-[[1S,2R]-2-hydroxy-2-(4-hydroxyphényle)-1-méthyléthyl]amino]éthyl]phénoxy]acétique ayant de puissants effets de stimulation du récepteur  beta 2-adrénergique et du récepteur  beta 3-adrénergique, utile pour soulager la douleur, favoriser l'élimination des calculs, etc., dans la lithiase urinaire, avec des crêtes de diffraction intense à 10,8, 19,1, 19,3, 19,8, 20,6 et 27 DEG  dans le diagramme du diffractomètre de rayons X sur poudre, à un angle de diffraction (2 theta +/-0,1). Il est possible d'obtenir ce produit, par exemple, en effectuant l'hydrolyse d'éthyle 2-[4-[2-[[1S,2R]-2-hydroxy-2-(4-hydroxyphényle)-1- méthyléthyl]amino]éthyl]phénoxy]acétate phosphate : à cet effet, on utilise de l'hydroxyde de sodium auquel il faut ajouter une solution aqueuse d'acide phosphorique à 40 DEG  C ou plus pour donner le composé susmentionné, avec adjonction d'un mélange solvant comprenant du méthanol et de l'eau, puis mélange en suspension à partir de 40 DEG  C jusqu'au point de reflux pendant une durée comprise entre 30 minutes et plusieurs heures.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>